{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "docs/ops/ods/CV1_CLOSURE_STATE_SCHEMA_v1.1.0.json",
  "title": "CV1_CLOSURE_STATE schema v1.1.0",
  "description": "Successor of CV1_CLOSURE_STATE_SCHEMA_v1.0.0.json (kept unchanged as history). Schema for docs/ops/ods/CV1_CLOSURE_STATE.json, a MUTABLE DERIVED PROJECTION: not authority, never outranking the authority, human decisions, certifications, provider observations or evidence it points at. A newer projection may change current dispositions but may not erase earlier evidence, findings, invalidators, certifications or lifecycle history. Governed by docs/ops/ods/ODS_V1_MAINTENANCE_ADDENDUM_v1.0.39.json (durable-source and per-edge dependency policies). scripts/ops/closure-state.ts interprets the structural subset below and reads every semantic token set from x-vocabulary and x-transition-graph; it hand-copies no enum.",
  "x-not-authority": true,
  "x-supersedes": "docs/ops/ods/CV1_CLOSURE_STATE_SCHEMA_v1.0.0.json",
  "x-semantic-rules": {
    "SHA_BINDING": "lifecycle >= AUTHORED requires candidate_sha, tree_sha, authority, authority_version; >= MATERIALIZED requires lineage_shas.materialization; >= EVIDENCED requires lineage_shas.evidence_head.",
    "DURABLE_SOURCE": "A durable fact is a REPOSITORY_FACT, INDEPENDENT_CERTIFICATION or HUMAN_DECISION item carrying ref, path, field AND value (re-checked by --verify-git). Free-text `source`, chat, memory, RUN_STATE or a value-less pointer is contextual only and never supports CERTIFIED, MATERIALIZED, ARMED, execution_allowed, CLOSED or a finding resolution.",
    "LIFECYCLE_HISTORY": "lifecycle_history replays x-transition-graph: first entry in initial_states; each later entry is exactly one forward edge with a durable basis of the edge's classes and ref binding, a rebind (same state, new candidate) only at rebind_states with a fired BINDING_CHANGED invalidator targeting the old candidate, or a regression with a fired invalidator. lifecycle_state and candidate_sha equal the last entry.",
    "CERTIFICATION_COHERENCE": "certification is null or the LAST certification_history entry; every history entry is INDEPENDENT with a durable INDEPENDENT_CERTIFICATION evidence item whose value equals its verdict; outcome agrees with the verdict by token suffix (never substring) and never mixes PASS with FAIL/BLOCKED/INSUFFICIENT tokens; certification_status is exactly the status mapped from outcome unless a fired invalidator targets the certification or the candidate moved without valid inheritance.",
    "LIFECYCLE_CERTIFICATION": "lifecycle >= CERTIFIED requires a PASS-class certification_status.",
    "CERTIFICATION_BINDING": "a PASS-class status must match authority_version and covered_package_digest recorded at certification; a certification on another SHA is valid only via certification_inherits_from with both package digests present and equal.",
    "FIRED_INVALIDATOR": "a fired invalidator targeting the current certification or candidate forbids a PASS-class status and execution_allowed; a fired observation invalidator forbids execution_allowed for its consumers. Fired invalidators need a target and fired_at.",
    "FRESHNESS": "an expired TTL (record or consumed observation) forbids execution_allowed=true and lifecycle >= ARMED.",
    "IMPLEMENTED_VS_INTEGRATED": "implementation_status and integration_status are independent; lifecycle >= MATERIALIZED requires an implementation-satisfied status regardless of integration_status.",
    "CERTIFICATION_SCOPE": "certification.scope=INTEGRATION and evidence scope INTEGRATED require integration_status=INTEGRATED.",
    "DEPENDENCY": "every dependency edge declares required_state and applies_from_state (no default); applies_from_state <= dependency_max_applies_from_state; when the record is at/after applies_from_state, at/after ARMED, or execution_allowed, the dependency's lifecycle must be >= required_state.",
    "FINDING_RESOLUTION": "RESOLVED or SUPERSEDED requires resolution_fact_id pointing at a durable evidence item; SUPERSEDED also requires superseded_by naming another finding of the record.",
    "CLOSED_REQUIRES": "lifecycle CLOSED requires every dependency requirement, no OPEN finding, and (via LIFECYCLE_HISTORY) a durable HUMAN_DECISION basis.",
    "EXECUTION_ALLOWED": "execution_allowed=true requires lifecycle ARMED, a PASS-class status, every dependency requirement, and no OPEN finding.",
    "EXECUTED_EVIDENCE": "lifecycle >= EXECUTED requires observed_at and at least one REPOSITORY_FACT or PROVIDER_OBSERVATION evidence item (INFERENCE alone never suffices).",
    "EVIDENCE_CLASS": "REPOSITORY_FACT needs ref+path; PROVIDER_OBSERVATION needs observation_id; INFERENCE needs derived_from; HUMAN_DECISION and INDEPENDENT_CERTIFICATION need source or ref+path; field needs ref+path.",
    "REFERENCES": "gate_ids unique; dependencies, observation consumers, basis facts and evidence observation_ids resolve; an observation's consumers are exactly the records that cite it; no two observations share provider+surface+projection+observed_at.",
    "NO_SECRET_MATERIAL": "no object key may be secret-bearing and no string may look like a credential or connection string; detected values are never printed.",
    "GENESIS": "with no previous projection (e.g. the base lacks the file), no record may end in genesis_forbidden_final_states; every record still replays its lifecycle_history.",
    "TRANSITION": "between revisions: revision +1, as_of non-decreasing; records, evidence items, findings, invalidators, dependency edges, observations, lifecycle_history and certification_history are never removed or rewritten (history is a prefix); a fired invalidator never unfires; appended history entries carry the new revision; a new record ends at most at new_record_max_final_state. A v1.0.0 previous is checked for the same identities (migration)."
  },
